  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Breeding of disease tolerant vegetable seed</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The pest Tuta absoluta is a major catastrophe for tomato growers in many developing counties in the Middle East and Northern Africa. Traditional chemical control measures are not very effective against this pest and alternative pest control has also its own conditions for effectiveness that can often not been met in these countries.For that reason Gebroeders Bakker Zaadteelt en Zaadhandel B.V. has decided to develop a hybrid tomato variety that is tolerant for this pest. They have decided to establish a seed breeding station in Jordan to work on this problem. As they have to set up a seed breeding station under local conditions they have decided to start a breeding programme for an egg plant variety that is Fusarium resistant as well.The project is interesting because of its contribution to agricultural knowledge development in Jordan, the development on breeding for resistance against and tolerance for plant diseases and pests opposed to chemical control and the involvement of local outgrowers.</narrative>
  </description>
